WEBVTT

NOTE ToonStudio product tour narration captions.

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:05.368
ToonStudio is more than a tool for drawing a
single image.

2
00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:21.712
From shaping an idea to finishing a manuscript
and preparing a series, it keeps the webtoon
workflow connected around one work.

3
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:39.960
Start in the browser, then move naturally
between planning, 2D and 3D production, review,
and publishing preparation.

4
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:52.392
The work begins in the Story Lab.

5
00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:07.548
First, define the world, characters, desires,
obstacles, and the principles that move the
story.

6
00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:28.748
Keep episode goals, scene intent, and key
dialogue in the production context so the next
drawing step becomes clearer.

7
00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:52.608
Now move into the drawing workspace.

8
00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:08.072
The canvas stays central, with brushes, layers,
selection, and frequently used tools close at
hand.

9
00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:34.192
Open texture, filters, and color correction only
when needed, keeping more room for the actual
manuscript.

10
00:02:55.000 --> 00:03:01.368
A scene becomes a readable story from the moment
you divide it into panels.

11
00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:17.940
Adjust balloons, dialogue, and the reader's eye
flow on the same manuscript,

12
00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:34.312
then check the vertical scroll pacing to
complete the scene's rhythm.

13
00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:55.512
When a composition is difficult, design the
scene first in the 3D workspace.

14
00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:15.688
Arrange character poses, backgrounds, and space,
then move the camera to explore angles quickly.

15
00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:43.128
Bring the chosen composition and camera changes
back into the current 2D manuscript. 3D is a
tool for finding a better scene.

16
00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:05.112
Now, let's step into the virtual studio.

17
00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:26.448
Walk the spaces of your work as your own
character, and check the mood and flow of each
scene for yourself.

18
00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:43.328
Shape the space with a classic stage and 3D
environments, and gather with your team in one
shared studio.

19
00:05:55.000 --> 00:06:00.552
The AI workspace reduces repetition and supports
idea exploration.

20
00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:16.472
Use your personal Creator Runtime and generation
tools,

21
00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:36.592
while keeping review, selection, and the final
decision to apply a result in the creator's
hands.

22
00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:55.608
In team production, share the current state of
the work instead of passing files around.

23
00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:14.680
See owners, production stages, and next actions
in the context of the actual work,

24
00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:36.728
then connect revision requests, change history,
and review results to reduce omissions and
bottlenecks.

25
00:07:55.000 --> 00:08:00.360
When work stalls, the learning area helps you
find the next useful action.

26
00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:19.832
Explore webtoon workflows, art and story
techniques, exercises, and references that lead
into real work,

27
00:08:28.500 --> 00:08:35.228
and find creative resources such as assets and
audio close to the production flow.

28
00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:50.208
At the finishing stage, review the manuscript
images, work information, and publishing
settings once more.

29
00:08:56.000 --> 00:09:03.232
Validate formats and required fields, then
finish export and publishing preparation in the
same work.

30
00:09:10.000 --> 00:09:15.192
Start where you need to, and carry the work all
the way through with ToonStudio.
